# Finalize local-diff review

When this turn asks for `<agenthub:review-verdict>`:

- **Always end the turn with the verdict block.** A turn without one is not
  recorded as "undecided" — the orchestrator scores it `review_failed` and
  Finalize stops with no review at all. There is no third value; withholding
  the block is strictly worse than either choice.
- Start from the attached review corpus (session rule / system-prompt file /
  stdin). If the prompt flags **Partial input**, that corpus is incomplete.
- If omitted patches are listed, read them. Your shell and file tools work —
  Cursor spawns run with `--sandbox disabled` precisely so those reads
  succeed. Hub `terminal` has no `op: exec`; use your own Read / Bash tools.
- If a read still fails, say so in the prose and decide on what you could see.
  A tool failure is **not** an implementation defect: do not score unread files
  as unmet acceptance criteria, and do not request changes because a command
  errored. State the gap plainly and let the human weigh it.
- `changes_requested` is for a defect you actually found and can point at.
  `approved` is for a review that found no blocker in what it read.
